[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "2607199950"
  :adr/title "cloud-itonami 5820 in-house deploy (LaunchAgent + cloudflared) + within-product maturity-loop close"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-19"
  :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki" "Claude Code (/loop)"]
  :adr/body
  "# Context\n\nThe maturity loop (ADR-2607189200) established that cloud-itonami's\nportfolio score is hard-gated on the first external paid conversion\n(externalPaid=0, owner/market action, not agent-movable) and pivoted to\nwithin-product maturity. The within-product demo-generation sweep is owned\nby a separate active effort (wave5, ADR-2607189300). This loop's\nnon-duplicative layer was the HTTP/governor surface of the http.clj actors\n(5820 / 6201 / 6202), which wave5 explicitly deferred.\n\nTwo improvement patterns were landed across all three http.clj actors:\n- POST /approve (escalation resume): closes the gap where /propose returned\n  202 escalated+thread-id but had no HTTP route to resume the\n  human-in-the-loop interrupt (the graph already supported resume via\n  g/run* {:thread-id .. :resume? true}). 5820 (iter5), 6202 (iter9), 6201 (iter10).\n- render-html (build-time operator-console): the build-time demo entrypoint\n  wave5 deferred for the http.clj shape. 5820 (iter11), 6202 (iter12), 6201 (iter13).\nBoth verified deterministic, real governed output, non-duplicative.\n\nThe remaining blocker for live effect was deploy: the 5820 CRM was not\nhosted anywhere (itonami.cloud/isic-5820/ serves the cockpit shell, not the\nCRM; the JVM app ran only in tests). Owner directive: deploy without Fly\n(「fly は使わない前提」).\n\n# Decision\n\nDeploy the 5820 CRM **in-house** as a local LaunchAgent + cloudflared named\ntunnel. Rejected alternatives:\n- **Fly**: owner-ruled-out. (Best JVM fit but external + needs auth.)\n- **cloud-murakumo / murakumo wasm lattice**: the 5820 is a full JVM app\n  (langgraph-clj StateGraph + http-kit + datomic/kotobase). The kotoba wasm\n  subset is at low-level capability-demo maturity (alloc/memory/host-sign/\n  notify); expressing a full HTTP CRM exceeds it. Re-architecture would\n  require advancing the kotoba wasm platform itself first — a separate\n  strategic project, not a deploy.\n- **Cloudflare Containers (open beta)**: autonomous (wrangler authed) but a\n  JVM app is a poor fit for serverless (slow startup, memory pressure).\n\nChosen: the established itonami-local pattern — every itonami routine runs\nas a macOS LaunchAgent. The 5820 JVM runs as a LaunchAgent (token read from\nkagi at launch, durable FileStore), fronted by a cloudflared named tunnel\n(also a LaunchAgent) exposing it at a stable hostname.\n\n# Outcome — the 5820 CRM is LIVE\n\n- Service: LaunchAgent com.gftdcojp.itonami-5820-serve (wrapper\n  ~/.gftd/run-itonami-5820-serve.sh -> clojure -M:dev:serve, port 8582,\n  ISIC5820_API_TOKEN from kagi, ISIC5820_STORE_FILE durable, KeepAlive).\n- Tunnel: LaunchAgent com.gftdcojp.itonami-5820-tunnel (cloudflared named\n  tunnel itonami-5820, 4962d03e-…, 3 edge connections nrt).\n- DNS: itonami-5820.etzhayyim.com -> tunnel (etzhayyim.com is cloudflared's\n  cert zone; itonami.cloud is a different zone not reachable from this\n  cloudflared cert).\n- Boot-persistent: plists copied to ~/Library/LaunchAgents/.\n- Verified externally: /health -> 200; full CRM round-trip\n  /propose (dispute) -> 202 escalated -> /approve -> committed (the iter5\n  /approve endpoint, now live).\n\nDeploy manifest: 90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-5820-deploy.toml.\n\n# Consequences\n\n- The iter5 /approve endpoint + the 5820 HTTP/governor stack are now live\n  (real effect, not just code maturity).\n- The dogfood (iter4 seed) is unblocked: the live CRM can now host\n  cloud-itonami's 4-vertical funnel. Next step is seeding the store with the\n  dogfood data (account creation is store-level, not a governed op).\n- Portfolio score stays at externalPaid=0 (deploy built the funnel\n  infrastructure; paid conversion is still the owner/market gate).\n- Mac-dependent: the CRM serves while the host is up. Acceptable for the\n  in-house/dogfood stage; a persistent-cloud host is a future upgrade if the\n  dogfood drives real demand.\n- The etzhayyim.com hostname (not itonami.cloud) is a zone-access artifact;\n  a production itonami.cloud hostname needs cloudflared cert for that zone\n  or wrangler-DNS management (follow-up, not blocking)."}]
